  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHome - Elections - Mahaska County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Mahaska County\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Mahaska County Elections\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPoll Workers\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to the Mahaska County Elections Website.\n The Election Department in the Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n Election Results\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n4\n \n \n\n City/School Election\n City/School Election\n \n\n Unofficial Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Update to City Clerk and School Secretary Duties\n \n July 16, 2026 \n\n \n \n\n Attestor Legislative Update\n \n \n\n Updated Voter Registration Form\n \n \nAll News\n \n \n\n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat do I need to bring with me to vote?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nStarting in January of 2019 you will be required to show identification. If you need to register to vote on Election Day, you must bring proof of identification and proof of residency. \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan a homeless person register to vote?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. Any eligible voter in Iowa may register to vote. Because many of those who are homeless have a nontraditional address they just need to provide an address or description of where they sleep the most, wherever that may be. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n\n \n \n\n \n Mahaska County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated May 29, 2026\n \n\n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n9,163\n \n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n5,991\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n3,222\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n153\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 18,529\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Mahaska County Auditor\n\n Mahaska County Courthouse, 1st Floor\n\n 106 South 1st Street\n\n Oskaloosa, Iowa 52577\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00AM to 4:30PM\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (641) 673-7148\n\n Fax: (641) 673-2597\n\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Mahaska County Elections\n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
